--[[
    .tradeval v15.2 (strict edition)  -  MM2 trade value watcher  (read-only except the optional AUTO-ACCEPT switch in CONFIG, which presses Accept on incoming trade requests)

    * TRADE   - both sides of the trade you open yourself, item icons, demand-weighted verdict
    * INV     - the total value of YOUR inventory with every item listed (sort / filter)
    * ADDS    - recommended items to ask for / add to make the trade fair or good
    * VALUES  - paste mm2values.txt / mm2values.csv once (Name / Value / Demand / Stability / DataID)
    * STYLE   - wallpaper, darkness + panel opacity, crest + colours, and the CUSTOM LUA STYLE box
    * CONFIG  - shading settings + VALUE MATCHING + AUTO-ACCEPT trade requests + DISCORD WEBHOOK
    * BEG     - bot that teleports to players, asks for a free weapon in chat ONCE per person, accepts their trade, waits, moves on
    * DEBUG   - raw GetTradeStatus payload, item metadata, owned items, inventory detection report, recent log
    * drag the header to move, drag any edge or corner to resize (any size), press 9 shows / hides  /  on mobile the round .tv button shows + hides it

    v15.2:
      - BEG: HOP AFTER TRADE switch - after one accepted trade the bot hops to a new random server.
      - CONFIG: DISCORD WEBHOOK is back - paste a channel webhook URL, SAVE, WEBHOOK ON.
             Sends one embed per server hop and per accepted BEG trade; TEST sends one now.
      - BEG: TEST HOP button - one immediate blind random hop (no HTTP / games API),
             still respecting a random minimum gap between teleport attempts.

    v14.9:
      - BEG: exactly one message per person (retried only if sending actually failed), then the next person gets one too
      - BEG: trade accept now uses TradeGUI.Container.Trade.Actions.Accept properly:
            waits for Accept.Cooldown to hide, presses Accept, then presses Accept.Confirm when it shows

    v14.8 STRICT DETECTION (no guessing, nothing inferred):
      - only ids that exist in the game's weapon database are ever accepted (inventory + trade)
      - a record without a numeric amount is skipped instead of being counted as 1
      - knife / gun is read ONLY from the explicit id text (_K / _G suffix, ...Knife / ...Gun ending)
        or the game metadata; if neither says, the item is not priced as a knife or gun
      - the release year comes ONLY from the id / name; an entry with a different year is never used
      - the holiday / event (Christmas, Halloween, Summer, Easter, Valentine's, Thanksgiving) is read
        ONLY when it is written in the id (Xmas..., Summer_Stickers..., ...) or the metadata, and is
        used for event-specific value names such as "Stickers Gun (Christmas 2021)"
      - an id such as "Stickers_K_2025" that fits several events is left unpriced, never guessed
      - names shared by several different game items are never auto-resolved
      - the inventory GUI fallback only reads labels that are actually on screen and only accepts
        names that belong to exactly one game item; quantities from the GUI are marked as unknown
      - CLOSEST name matching is OFF by default (and is switched off once for older saved settings)
      - values are exact name matches only: name + kind + year + event, then name + rarity tag

    Network: the only external request is an image download for the wallpaper.
    Settings are saved to your executor workspace: mm2_trade_watcher_settings.json
]]

